From 8ff1e422d5237b9d14e84cc14b484b00ba69e20e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: a game test's diagnostics: the memory call log, the
 first guest exception's memory dump, the aligned rest switch

EDEN_PS4_MEM_LOG=1: SetHeapSize, Map/UnmapPhysicalMemory (with the physical pieces each mapping
got), Map/UnmapMemory, SetMemoryPermission/Attribute and the memory GetInfos, with their results, in
log.txt (the first 6000; GetInfo's 400); at the first guest exception that isn't a hint, what its
registers point at (block, physical page, bytes) and the memory map. EDEN_PS4_ALIGNED_REST=0: Eden's
own single pages for an allocation's rest under 64 KiB, in place of the PS4's 16 KiB-aligned run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W5pLthrq7391gS4qodPV4u
